<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for sharedchats.com: no accounts, no personal data collection, consent-based Google Analytics, and your rights under Indian data protection law."
  lastUpdated="July 26, 2026"
>
  <p>
    SharedChats is a static website. There are no accounts, no sign-ups, no comment boxes, and no
    forms. We do not collect, store, or sell personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics (only with your consent)</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics 4 to understand aggregate traffic — which pages are popular and roughly
    where visitors come from. Analytics loads <strong>only after you accept</strong> the cookie
    banner. If you decline, no analytics cookies are set and nothing is tracked. Google Analytics is
    configured with IP truncation, and we never see individual identities.
  </p>

  <h2>Withdrawing consent</h2>
  <p>
    Your choice is stored in your browser's local storage. To withdraw consent, clear this site's
    data in your browser settings — the banner will ask again on your next visit, and you can
    decline. You can also email us and we will explain the steps.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to request access to, correction of, or erasure of any personal data
    concerning you. Because we don't collect personal data, such requests will usually be about
    content in a listed conversation — we handle those as removal requests and act promptly. Write
    to <a href="mailto:hello@sharedchats.com">hello@sharedchats.com</a> for any of these requests.
  </p>

  <h2>Grievance redressal</h2>
  <p>
    For grievances under applicable Indian data protection law (including the Digital Personal Data
    Protection Act), contact <a href="mailto:hello@sharedchats.com">hello@sharedchats.com</a>.
    Designated grievance-officer details will be published here as required.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If our data practices ever change — for example, if we add a submission form — this policy will
    be updated first, and the "Last updated" date will reflect it.
  </p>
</Legal>
